  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Commercial Vehicle Group is experiencing uneven demand across its portfolio, with solid momentum in Global Electrical Systems and Seating offset by persistent softness in Trim Systems and Components. The return to consolidated revenue growth signals a stabilization, but the divergence across product lines suggests that certain end-markets remain under pressure while others benefit from secular trends like electrification and comfort upgrades. External macro uncertainty continues to weigh on the broader commercial vehicle cycle, yet the company’s exposure to recovering segments is providing a buffer.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is balancing near-term operational discipline with balance-sheet strengthening. A sale-leaseback transaction accelerated leverage reduction, demonstrating a proactive approach to capital allocation. Management reaffirmed full-year guidance that sits above consensus, signaling confidence in the trajectory despite mixed end-market signals. The focus on operational efficiency is yielding sequential margin improvements, and the team is effectively steering through a fragmented recovery by leaning into higher-growth product lines while keeping a tight grip on costs.",
